{
    /* A matrix product, contracted in one flow.

       A is 2x3 and B is 3x4. Viewing them as [2,3,1] and [1,3,4] lines their
       shared axis up: a length-1 axis stretches against a longer one, so the
       product below spans [2,3,4]. Folding away axis 1 contracts it to [2,4].

       Hand the kernel one pointer per space when you call it — the order is
       the one rho_kernel_metadata() lists, and nothing is baked in:

         engine.execute_spaces({"A": a, "B": b, "OUTPUT": c})   # rho.py
         rho_kernel_exec_spaces((void *[]){a, b, c});           // C

       Or bind the addresses at compile time and call rho_kernel_exec():

         rhoc examples/matmul.rho --bind A=0x... --bind B=0x... --bind OUTPUT=0x...
    */
    A:◯ □ 2 3 1
    B:◯ □ 1 3 4

    ◇+1 (A × B) → OUTPUT

    OUTPUT → =
}
